<title>NORWAY: NCL buys Kvaerner ship $110 mln.</title>
<headline>NCL buys Kvaerner ship $110 mln.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian Cruise Lines (NCL) said on Wednesday it had agreed to buy the Royal Majesty cruise liner from Kvaerner ASA as part of its expansion plans.</p>
<p>The company said it had paid $110 million for the ship, goodwill and the rights to enter Bermuda. It also handed over 19.9 percent of the stock in NCL Cruises Ltd, a subsidiary of NCL Holdings.</p>
